{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The dispute is flagged safety-related and the trip record carries the safety indicator itself — the rider's own in-app message at 01:41:36, 'Please slow down, you are driving very fast and I feel scared' — so POL-GEN-21 requires this case to go to human review whatever category the filer chose: the AI may not issue a refund, find fault or recommend a resolution, and the 38.51 SGD charged is held rather than returned while a human reviews the file.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05013"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-21"],
      "relies_on": "dispute.safety_flag",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "On the money, the rider's demand of 8.00 SGD exceeds anything the refund matrix can produce: the deviation is 1.90 km (actual 24.3 km less recommended 22.4 km) and the base per-km rate is 0.72 SGD, so the entire excess distance fare under POL-RD-24 is 1.37 SGD — that figure, and not 8.00, is the ceiling of the rider's monetary claim on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05013", "EV-FARE-05013"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-24"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.deviation.deviation_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver-device trace that recorded this trip is graded COMPLETE at weight 1.0 with no issue codes, carries 54 fixes at 30-second intervals from trip start to trip end with no gap, and shows the vehicle on mapped roads — PIE, then Loyang Avenue and Loyang Way, rejoining the recommended route at Pasir Ris Close / Pasir Ris Drive 3 at 01:44:03 — a continuous, on-network drive to the booked dropoff, with the pre-pass raising no speed anomaly.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-05013"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-22", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "gps_trace.derived.v7.point_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "To the extent the rider's complaint is that 'the fare was also higher', that is a fare and surge matter: the 38.51 SGD charged includes 12.54 SGD of surge at a 1.5 multiplier, and fare and surge disputes are not adjudicated by the AI in this version but routed to human review under POL-GEN-24 — so the fare-level element of this claim cannot ground an AI refund.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05013"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-24"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.surge_amount",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
